  status: active
  ratified_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-10-17T05:51:42Z
  summary: Clarify symbol-link parsing and correct Link's code-name metadata.
  rationale: Symbol fingerprint modes require a clean parse of the whole file; byte fingerprints do not parse source syntax. Replace the misleading JSON-as-invalid-Python example with an actual syntax-error case and a byte-mode boundary. Reference is a conceptual distinction, not an existing code name, so keep it in prose rather than the not list.
  establishes: []
  changes:
  - LINKS-001
  retires: []
  terms:
  - Link
- id: D261017-q54ty
  timestamp: 2026-10-17T00:30:57Z
  actor: user
  status: active
  ratified_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-10-17T00:39:26Z
  summary: Add manual checks for rule meaning, agent proposals and human approval, and strengthen the corresponding mechanical tests.
  rationale: Automated tests can check case metadata and CLI lifecycle transitions, but cannot judge whether a requirement is meaningful, an agent presents work honestly, or a person explicitly approved a specific decision. Keep partial mechanical tests unlinked until mixed automated and manual verification is supported; track that limitation as a high priority Beans bug. Preserve the existing rule statements and fully automated coverage for CORE-002 and LINKS-001.
  establishes: []
  changes:
  - CORE-001
  - CORE-004
  - CORE-005
  retires: []
  terms: []
- id: D261017-4zy7n
  timestamp: 2026-10-17T05:28:33Z
  actor: agent
  status: active
  ratified_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-10-17T05:51:42Z
  summary: 'Record the history and stale-link guarantees that let Statute keep rules true: active decisions are immutable, agreed rules and terms change only with a decision, changed targets make links stale, and only a review verdict refreshes them.'
  rationale: These are the checks behind the one-pager's promise that nobody quietly edits a rule to match the code and that a change to linked code or tests brings the rule up for review. Each rule gets a dedicated contract test so its test link changes only when its own cases change. Base, Stale link and Missing link are the vocabulary these rules and the CLI output use.
  establishes:
  - HIST-001
  - HIST-002
  - HIST-003
  - LINKS-002
  - LINKS-003
  changes: []
  retires: []
  terms:
  - Base
  - Stale link
  - Missing link
- id: D261017-rlpdd
  timestamp: 2026-10-17T06:06:51Z
  actor: agent
  status: active
  ratified_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-10-17T21:24:06Z
  summary: 'Record the missing-link, broken-rule and decision-lifecycle guarantees: a gone or ambiguous target is missing until relinked, a built rule with an open gap is broken, a rule or term is in at most one proposed decision, and ratify activates exactly the named decisions or writes nothing.'
  rationale: 'These checks keep a broken or unapproved state from being cleared quietly: review cannot clear a missing link, broken follows the gaps file, overlapping proposals cannot be approved by accident, and ratify never agrees more than the person approved or leaves an invalid result. Each area has a dedicated contract test. Fingerprint, Draft rule and Proposed decision are the vocabulary the CLI and these rules use.'
  establishes:
  - LINKS-004
  - GAPS-001
  - DEC-001
  - DEC-002
  - DEC-003
  changes: []
  retires: []
  terms:
  - Fingerprint
  - Draft rule
  - Proposed decision
